From f9b0b6c112cee0450b67f8b00fdc4a8b20e652aa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mesa-nvk-horizon <mesa-nvk-horizon@localhost>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 13:07:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 16/22] vulkan/runtime: include dlfcn.h only where it is
 actually used
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

vk_instance.c includes dlfcn.h on every platform that is not Windows,
but the only two things it uses from it — dlopen() and dlsym() — are
both inside #if HAVE_RENDERDOC_INTEGRATION. A C library with no dynamic
loader has no dlfcn.h at all, so the file failed to compile over a
header it did not need:

  vk_instance.c:42:10: fatal error: dlfcn.h: No such file or directory

The include is now gated on the same condition as the calls, plus
HAVE_DLOPEN: a platform could have the header and not the loader, and
what decides whether the calls can work is whether dlopen exists.
meson.build already computes that.

Nothing changes where RenderDoc integration is enabled, and nothing
changes on Windows.

mesa-nvk-horizon: Phase 4 — the nouveau Vulkan driver for Horizon
Why: newlib/libnx has no dynamic loader, so no dlfcn.h (patch 0001
  records dlopen, libdl and dlfcn.h all measured absent).
Evidence: building mesa-26.1.5 for aarch64/horizon with
  -Dvulkan-drivers=nouveau stopped at the fatal error quoted above.
  With this change the file compiles.
Upstream: yes — it narrows an include to the code that uses it and is
  a no-op wherever that code is built.
---
 src/vulkan/runtime/vk_instance.c | 15 +++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/vulkan/runtime/vk_instance.c b/src/vulkan/runtime/vk_instance.c
index 420ab21..c78a0cf 100644
--- a/src/vulkan/runtime/vk_instance.c
+++ b/src/vulkan/runtime/vk_instance.c
@@ -38,7 +38,18 @@
 #include "compiler/glsl_types.h"
 #endif
 
-#ifndef _WIN32
+/* dlfcn.h is included for the RenderDoc integration and for nothing
+ * else: the two uses below, dlopen() and dlsym(), are both inside
+ * #if HAVE_RENDERDOC_INTEGRATION. Gating the include on the same thing
+ * keeps a C library with no dynamic loader — which therefore has no
+ * dlfcn.h at all — from failing to compile a file that would not have
+ * called into it anyway.
+ *
+ * HAVE_DLOPEN as well as the RenderDoc flag: a platform could in
+ * principle have the header and not the loader, and the check that
+ * matters for the calls is whether dlopen exists.
+ */
+#if HAVE_RENDERDOC_INTEGRATION && defined(HAVE_DLOPEN) && !defined(_WIN32)
 #include "dlfcn.h"
 #endif
 
@@ -651,7 +662,7 @@ vk_icdNegotiateLoaderICDInterfaceVersion(uint32_t *pSupportedVersion)
 void
 vk_instance_start_renderdoc_capture(struct vk_instance *instance)
 {
-#if HAVE_RENDERDOC_INTEGRATION
+#if HAVE_RENDERDOC_INTEGRATION && defined(HAVE_DLOPEN)
    simple_mtx_lock(&instance->renderdoc_mtx);
 
    if (!instance->renderdoc_api) {
